  <wpt lat="46.625967" lon="7.206881">
    <name>Charmey - Vounetse (Gruyère) [36 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <desc>Vounetse 1627 m - top of the Charmey gondola

Trails
No purpose-built bike park - this is old-school alpine riding. From Vounetse you drop through open pasture on alp tracks, then into forest singletrack back to Charmey, with the Dents Vertes restaurant as the obvious mid-ride stop. Quiet, scenic, and a good option when the bike parks are heaving on a Saturday.

Getting up / price
Gondola day ticket 36 CHF adult (25-63), 31 CHF for 16-24, free under 6. Free with the Magic Pass.

Open season
Open from 15 May; closed from 2 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h40

Source: Charmey. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.154468" lon="6.193165">
    <name>Le Salève (above Geneva) [18 EUR return]</name>
    <desc>Salève 1100 m - top of the Veyrier cable car

Trails
Mountain biking is only allowed on the dedicated marked trails here - the Saleve is a nature-protection area and the rules are enforced, so stick to the signed descents towards Veyrier, Monnetier and Collonges-sous-Saleve. Short runs (roughly 600 m of vertical) but you can lap them cheaply and the trails stay ridable very late into autumn.

Getting up / price
13 EUR one way, 18 EUR return; bikes travel in the cabin at no extra charge. Under 5 minutes to 1100 m.

Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h25

Source: Saleve cable car. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.314928" lon="7.385609">
    <name>Anzère - Pas de Maimbré [bikes ride free]</name>
    <desc>Pas-de-Maimbré 2362 m - top of the Anzère gondola

Trails
One marked downhill line plus four signed routes totalling around 80 km. The DH starts from the Pas de Maimbre or from the mid station, picks up just below La Dent and finishes at the bottom of the Masques trail - about 380 m of continuous descent on the steep part. High, open and dry: a good choice in a wet spell lower down.

Getting up / price
Carrying a mountain bike on the gondola is free in summer, which makes this unusually good value; you only pay your own passenger ticket. Anzere is a Magic Pass resort.

Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h50

Source: Anzere tourism. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.139139" lon="7.214443">
    <name>Bienne / Magglingen - BielTrail [16 CHF with Half Fare]</name>
    <desc>Magglingen/Macolin - top of the funicular

Trails
BielTrail is a 1.95 km, 440 m descent running point-to-point back towards the funicular. Most of the main line is fast, flowing and well maintained, but it includes a short black section that is genuinely technical: a steep downhill passage through rocks and roots. Additional, more relaxed paths descend through the same area, but these are shared with hikers rather than bike-only trails: slow down, give way and expect people around blind corners. The wider Jura network (Les Pres-d'Orvin Bike 844, Erguel Bike 843) starts from the same plateau if you want more distance.

Getting up / price
The Magglingen funicular is part of Biel city transport. A day costs 16 CHF with the Swiss Half Fare Travelcard, making repeated laps unusually good value. There is a bike wash behind the lower funicular station.

Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year; avoid riding when the ground is saturated and check local conditions.
Daily opening hours: 05:45-00:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + funicular | ~1h25

Source: City of Biel. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
