  <wpt lat="46.091099" lon="7.252660">
    <name>Verbier - 4 Vallées [47 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Les Ruinettes 2200 m - bike park top

Trails
Verbier Bike Park by Commencal: the most serious lift-served downhill within two hours of Lausanne. Long, steep, properly rough World-Cup-adjacent lines off Les Ruinettes and La Chaux, plus a huge natural enduro network reaching down 1500 m to Le Chable. Savoleyres is the quieter side with more natural, flowy trails. Bring a real bike and pads.

Getting up / price
Verbier bike day pass 47 CHF; the full 4 Vallees bike day pass 57 CHF. Season: Verbier 229 CHF, 4 Vallees 329 CHF. Le Chable &gt; Verbier return is 12.80 CHF and Verbier &gt; Les Ruinettes return 25 CHF if you only want one lap. 10% off online 10+ days ahead. Main summer season 4 July - 21 September 2026.

Open season
Open from 4 July; closed from 22 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~1h50

Source: Verbier 4 Vallees. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.103794" lon="7.224809">
    <name>Verbier: Savoleyres - second lift, quieter enduro side</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.368666" lon="7.648433">
    <name>Leukerbad - Torrent [~40 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Rinderhütte 2350 m - top of the Torrent cable car

Trails
A well-signed Valais trail network rather than a bike park. Torrenttrail Bike (114) is the long one off the Rinderhutte; Chällerflue Bike (116) and the Deleeschi and Jales Flow flowtrails give you a mix of natural and built riding. High, sunny and dry, with thermal baths at the bottom - the best recovery of any spot on this list.

Getting up / price
Torrent-Bahnen day tickets - price not verified here, budget 35-45 CHF; check torrent.ch before travelling.

Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~2h05

Source: Leukerbad. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
