  <wpt lat="45.009907" lon="6.126549">
    <name>Les Deux Alpes (Isere, FR) [33 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Jandri / Vallee Blanche sector - lift hub

Trails
98 km of marked trails and one of the biggest lift-served verticals in Europe - over 2000 m from the glacier down to Venosc. Everything from wide green flow to raw World Cup black, plus the Vallee Blanche run. Les 2 Alpes is the venue of Mountain of Hell, a mass start race from the glacier that sends hundreds of riders onto snow, high-alpine trail and the long descent toward the valley.

Getting up / price
Bike park day pass 33 EUR adult, 4 hours 26 EUR, 2 days 57 EUR. Season 320 EUR, or 345 EUR for the three-area pass shared with Alpe d'Huez and La Grave. Trails open 11 April - 30 August 2026, daily from 13 June, with Thursday night riding until 22:30 between 9 July and 27 August.

Open season
Open from 11 April; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Grenoble | Car | ~1h10
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~6h

Sources: Les 2 Alpes and Mountain of Hell. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
