  <wpt lat="45.114380" lon="6.119995">
    <name>Alpe d'Huez (Grandes Rousses) [25 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Marmottes 3 - top station under the Pic Blanc

Trails
Enormous: 45 routes over roughly 300 km of marked trail and 2610 m of vertical from the Pic Blanc at 3330 m down to 1450 m. Alpe d'Huez is the venue of Megavalanche, the iconic mass start race that launches riders together from the Pic Blanc glacier into a marathon descent to Allemond. The built lines around the resort cover everything - Marmotland and Easy Rider for beginners, the Rif Nel flow trail and Central Park for jumps, Hot Road and Run DMC when you want speed. Above them sits a high-alpine descent that is genuinely one of the longest in Europe.

Getting up / price
MTB day pass 25 EUR adult, 21.50 EUR child, 21.50 EUR each on a family pass, 7.50 EUR over 72. Season 27 June - 30 August 2026, with a pre-opening on the weekend of 27-28 June.

Open season
Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Grenoble | Car | ~1h15

Sources: Alpe d'Huez and Megavalanche. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
