  <wpt lat="46.661377" lon="8.052960">
    <name>Grindelwald - First [Firstbahn, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>First 2168 m - top of the Firstbahn

Trails
15 km and 1100 m of descent from First back to Grindelwald on natural paths and tracks, under the north face of the Eiger the whole way. Not a built bike park - this is a big mountain descent with a gondola instead of a climb, and it splits naturally at Bort if you want a shorter day.

Getting up / price
Firstbahn gondola. Bike carriage and the exact 2026 fare are not confirmed here - check jungfrau.ch. Adventure packages bundling unlimited gondola use with activities are usually the better value if you are staying.

Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~3h00

Source: Grindelwald-First. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.646756" lon="8.051765">
    <name>Grindelwald: Bort</name>
    <desc>Mid station. The short Bort-to-village descent is the easy option if the full 1100 m looks like too much.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.625023" lon="8.041783">
    <name>Grindelwald: Firstbahn valley station</name>
    <desc>In the village, a few minutes from Grindelwald Terminal and the trains.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.656424" lon="8.621960">
    <name>Andermatt - Gemsstock / Gutsch [bike pass, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Gutsch 2344 m - top of the Gutsch-Express

Trails
High, bare and properly alpine - the SkiArena runs from the Gemsstock at nearly 3000 m across the Oberalp to Sedrun. The riding here is route-based rather than park-based: Oberalp Bike (205) is the classic loop over the pass, and Cavorgia Bike (207) carries on towards Sedrun. Add the Gottardo Bike and Furka Bike stages and you have a week of it. Little shelter and a short season: it can snow in August.

Getting up / price
Andermatt+Sedrun+Disentis sells summer bike and hiking day passes; check andermatt-sedrun-disentis.ch for price. Their half-price card covers summer bike day passes as well as winter skiing if you go more than once.

Open season
Open from 27 June; closed from 5 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~4h15

Source: Andermatt. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.602310" lon="8.611604">
    <name>Andermatt: Gemsstock</name>
    <desc>The high cable car, 2961 m. Bike carriage is not a given up here - ask before you queue.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.636840" lon="8.593329">
    <name>Andermatt: railway station</name>
    <desc>Matterhorn Gotthard Bahn and the Glacier Express. The Gutsch-Express valley station is a few minutes away.</desc>
  </wpt>
