  <wpt lat="46.391337" lon="8.067003">
    <name>Aletsch Arena - Riederalp / Bettmeralp / Fiescheralp [cable cars, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Bettmeralp - car-free village above the Rhone

Trails
A high sunny terrace above the Rhone valley, looking straight at the Aletsch glacier. The Flowtrail Wurzenbord is the built one; otherwise this is big-view touring, linking Riederalp, Bettmeralp and Martisberg, or pushing on from Fiescheralp to the Marjela. Not steep-and-gnarly country, but among the best scenery on this map, and easy to reach from Brig.

Getting up / price
Three separate cable cars from the valley floor - Morel to Riederalp, Betten to Bettmeralp, Fiesch to Fiescheralp - all run all year because the villages are car-free and have no road. Bike carriage is normal here; check aletscharena.ch for bike fare before travelling.

Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~2h15

Source: Aletsch Arena. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
