  <wpt lat="46.772374" lon="6.466241">
    <name>Le Suchet (Jura vaudois) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Le Suchet 1588 m - summit

Trails
Open Jura ridge with descents falling off every side - grassy and fast on the Vaud slope, rockier and steeper towards Baulmes. No signage, no lift queue, big views over the Plateau to the Alps. Best in early summer before the cattle churn the tracks.

Getting up / price
No lift. Yverdon-les-Bains is 25 min from Lausanne, then a bus to Baulmes or Vuiteboeuf. From there it is roughly 800 m of climbing under your own steam.

Open season
Open from 15 April; closed from 16 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h15

Source: Swiss federal map. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.572227" lon="6.276140">
    <name>Grand Cunay / Col du Marchairuz [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Grand Cunay 1566 m

Trails
Classic Jura vaudois ridge riding above the Vallee de Joux. Rolling limestone pasture, dry-stone walls and forest singletrack, with long low-gradient descents rather than steep ones. Quiet on weekdays; the Parc Jura vaudois rules ask you to stay on the tracks.

Getting up / price
No lift, and a sparse bus timetable: check the Bière or Le Brassus connections to the Col du Marchairuz before committing. Many people ride up from Bière instead.

Open season
Open from 15 April; closed from 16 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h30

Source: Swiss federal map. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.851795" lon="6.538253">
    <name>Le Chasseron (Sainte-Croix) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Le Chasseron 1607 m - summit

Trails
Long grassy ridge descents with one of the best panoramas in the Jura - the whole Alpine chain on a clear day. Fast and flowing up high, forest tracks lower down towards Sainte-Croix or Bullet. Pairs well with Le Suchet if you want a big day.

Getting up / price
No lift. Lausanne &gt; Yverdon 25 min &gt; Sainte-Croix 35 min, then about 600 m of climbing from Les Rasses.

Open season
Open from 15 April; closed from 16 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~1h10

Source: Yverdon region. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.565724" lon="6.692604">
    <name>Chalet-a-Gobet / Jorat (Lausanne) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Chalet-a-Gobet - Jorat forest trailhead

Trails
The after-work option: a dense web of forest doubletrack and singletrack across the Jorat, ridable in any weather and floodlit by nothing at all, so bring lights in winter. No descents worth travelling for, but 20 minutes from your door and the trails drain well.

Getting up / price
No lift and none needed - it is only 400 m above the city. Bus 64 from Lausanne, or the m2 to Croisettes and pedal up.

Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year; check local conditions.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Bus / metro + bus | ~25 min

Source: Lausanne tourism. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.688440" lon="7.310960">
    <name>Pila Bike Park (Aosta Valley) [40 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Pila 1790 m - Aosta-Pila gondola top station

Trails
A large, natural-feeling gravity area above Aosta with more than 130 km of riding and 2100 m of vertical. The official 2026 park lists one blue flow trail, twelve red descents, three black trails and the black Corrado Herin World Cup line, plus the long freeride descent back to Aosta.

Getting up / price
The 2026 adult bike pass is 40 EUR and includes bike transport. The Aosta-Pila gondola and bike park run daily from 13 June to 13 September 2026; Chamole opens from 20 June.

Open season
Open from 13 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
