  <wpt lat="45.886235" lon="6.753107">
    <name>Les Houches Bike Park (Chamonix Valley) [40.50 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Prarion 1850 m - gondola top station

Trails
Lift-served riding at the quieter western end of the Chamonix valley. The Prarion sector has blue, red and black downhill lines, including the 4 km Chamois black run with 640 m of descent. The same valley pass also reaches the larger Balme network, which has six marked trails from blue to black.

Getting up / price
The 2026 whole-valley MTB day pass is 40.50 EUR and gives uphill access at Les Houches and Balme. A Les Houches-only pass is 29.40 EUR. Summer riding is restricted to marked MTB routes in July and August.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; In July and August, ride only the marked MTB routes under the local municipal rules.
Open season
Open from 13 June; closed from 21 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Geneva | Car | ~1h10
Chamonix | Train + bus | ~30 min

Source: Les Houches. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
