  <wpt lat="45.597350" lon="6.795010">
    <name>Les Arcs Bike Park (Bourg-Saint-Maurice) [30 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Arc 1600, 1620 m - funicular arrival and Cachette lift hub

Trails
More than 150 km of marked riding across Les Arcs and Peisey-Vallandry: seven dedicated downhill trails, eight enduro routes and six e-MTB, cross-country and gravel routes. There is a green learning area and easy lines, while Cachette, La 8 and Dre dans l'Pentu provide long, technical black descents.

Getting up / price
The peak-season 2026 adult bike-park day pass is 30 EUR and covers twelve lifts. The mountain area runs from 13 June to 13 September 2026, with the full network operating from 4 July to 29 August; preview and late-season lift coverage is reduced.

Open season
Open from 13 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Geneva | Car | ~2h30
Bourg-Saint-Maurice | Funicular | ~7 min

Source: Les Arcs. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
