  <wpt lat="44.065590" lon="7.226970">
    <name>La Colmiane: Pic chairlift base (Col Saint-Martin, 1470 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="43.803110" lon="7.423330">
    <name>Col de la Madone / Ravin du Rank (above Menton) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Col de la Madone 925 m - road pass above Menton

Trails
Not a park: one serious trail, and a famous road climb to reach it. The Ravin du Rank drops off the col towards Gorbio, 2.8 km for 550 m of descent, graded T5 with E2 exposure - loose, brittle limestone and long sequences of built stone steps that will find the limits of your suspension and your nerve. Ridden downhill only; walking back up means carrying the bike the whole way. Sea views the entire descent, and ridable in January.

Getting up / price
Nothing to pay and nothing to ride up in. The col is the road climb the pros use for testing, about 900 m of ascent from Menton by Sainte-Agnes or by Peille. Shuttling by car is the usual alternative.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; T5 and exposed. Scout the step sections on foot before you commit - this is not a graded bike park run.
Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year; check local conditions.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Menton | Bike | ~1h15 climb
Nice | Car | ~50 min

Source: VTTour Ravin du Rank. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
