  <wpt lat="46.280700" lon="10.832340">
    <name>Val di Sole Bike Park (Daolasa, Trentino) [46 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Val Mastellina 2040 m - top of the Daolasa gondola

Trails
The World Cup venue, and host of the 2026 World Championships. Four marked runs plus a four-cross track share 550 m of vertical: White Wolf is the blue, Golden Eagle and Wild Grizzly the reds, and Black Snake the black - a downhill course cut by Pippo Marani and widely counted among the steepest and most technical on the circuit. Golden Eagle was rebuilt for 2026 and Black Snake gained a new diagonal and counter-slope section.

Getting up / price
The 8-seat Daolasa - Val Mastellina gondola runs from Commezzadura in the valley floor. Bike day pass 46 EUR adult, 32 EUR junior, 23 EUR child. Open 27 June to 13 September 2026. The park joined the Gravity Card circuit in 2026, so that pass works here too.

Open season
Open from 27 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Trento | Car | ~1h15
Milan | Car | ~3h00

Source: Val di Sole Bikeland. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.319180" lon="10.836200">
    <name>Val di Sole: Daolasa gondola valley station (815 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.097320" lon="-122.953260">
    <name>Whistler Mountain Bike Park (British Columbia) [season pass 999 CAD]</name>
    <desc>Fitzsimmons Express top 1020 m - the bike park's main unload

Trails
The one every other bike park is measured against. Around eighty machine-built and natural trails over four zones: Fitzsimmons for the famous flow - A-Line, Dirt Merchant, Crank It Up - Garbanzo above it for longer and steeper, Creekside for the quiet side, and the Peak zone for Top of the World, a high alpine descent of roughly 1500 m. Green jump lines through to double-black tech, and the trail crew rebuilds constantly. Whistler hosts the penultimate 2026 UCI Downhill World Cup, adding top-level racing to its established Crankworx festival role.

Getting up / price
The Fitzsimmons Express chair lifts riders out of Whistler Village; Garbanzo, Creekside and the Peak chair extend the terrain as the season opens up. The park runs mid-May to mid-October, with the Peak zone typically only from July to early September. The adult bike-park season pass is 999 CAD. Single-day pricing varies by date and advance purchase.

Open season
Open from 15 May; closed from 16 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-20:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Vancouver | Car | ~2h00

Sources: Whistler Bike Park, bike-park passes and 2026 UCI calendar. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.112850" lon="-122.953320">
    <name>Whistler: bike park base, Whistler Village (685 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.078990" lon="-122.951080">
    <name>Whistler: Garbanzo Express top (1680 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.087040" lon="-70.931760">
    <name>Mont-Sainte-Anne (Quebec) [gondola, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Summit 800 m - top of L'Etoile Filante gondola

Trails
North America's oldest World Cup downhill hill, and still one of its most punishing: the mountain's reputation is built on wet granite, roots and off-camber rock rather than machine-built berms. About 615 m of vertical under the gondola, roughly thirty downhill runs from beginner-graded flow to the World Cup track, and a cross-country and singletrack network that brings the mountain's total to around 175 km. It joined the Crankworx circuit as the 2026 World Tour finale.

Getting up / price
L'Etoile Filante gondola carries bikes to the summit; two chairlifts serve the lower mountain. Summer day tickets are sold through the resort's own ticket site and we could not confirm a 2026 mountain-bike rate, so check mont-sainte-anne.com before you go.

Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 16 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Quebec City | Car | ~35 min

Source: Mont-Sainte-Anne. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.074380" lon="-70.908490">
    <name>Mont-Sainte-Anne: gondola base (180 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.951352" lon="33.298047">
    <name>Machairas - Lythrodontas (Cyprus) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Machairas Forest mountain-bike hub from Lythrodontas

Trails
Cyprus's strongest documented mountain-bike area combines long rough dirt tracks, pine forest, sudden technical descents and substantial climbing around Kionia, Machairas Monastery and Mantra tou Kampiou. The area hosts major MTB races, but it is a natural route network rather than a gravity park.

Getting up / price
Free and pedal-accessed; no lift. The official 45 km circular route gains about 890 m and is rated very difficult. Guided e-MTB trips are available locally.

Open season
Open from 01 October; closed from 01 June (best cooler-season window; access may be possible year-round).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Summer heat and fire restrictions can affect forest access; check locally.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Nicosia | Car | ~40 min
Larnaca | Car | ~45 min

Sources: Visit Cyprus circular route and the Machairas route guide. Follow current forestry rules.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.922037" lon="32.880740">
    <name>Troodos Mountain Bike Routes (Cyprus) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Highland riding around Troodos Square and Mount Olympus

Trails
The Troodos cycling network mixes paved connectors, rough mining and forest roads, and natural mountain descents through pine forest and exposed ophiolite geology. It is best treated as adventure/enduro touring rather than a signed downhill park.

Getting up / price
No documented summer bike uplift. Ride from Troodos Square or build pedal/shuttle routes with a local guide; winter ski lifts should not be assumed to carry bikes.

Open season
Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free riding window).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Check forestry closures, heat, fire risk and route legality before riding.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Limassol | Car | ~55 min
Nicosia | Car | ~1h15

Sources: Troodos UNESCO Global Geopark and the official Visit Cyprus cycling guide. Confirm current access locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="33.984282" lon="35.847454">
    <name>Mzaar Mountain Resort MTB (Lebanon) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <desc>Summer mountain-bike trails at Mzaar Kfardebian

Trails
Lebanon's largest mountain resort advertises summer MTB trails designed for speed, mountain exploration and full-day riding. Expect open limestone terrain, high ridges and natural resort tracks rather than a fully documented modern downhill park.

Getting up / price
