    <name>Metabief - Mont d'Or (Jura, FR) [26.90 EUR / Magic Pass]</name>
    <desc>Morond 1410 m - top of the Morond chairlift

Trails
The biggest bike park in the eastern Jura, and the nearest real downhill to Lausanne. Eight marked downhill and enduro runs share about 390 m of vertical off the Morond, roughly 25 km of trail in total: dark spruce forest, roots and off-camber limestone rather than manicured berms, which makes the reds and blacks ride harder than the modest drop suggests. It rides best in the dry.

Getting up / price
The Morond chairlift carries bikes, usually 9h30 to 17h30. Day pass 26.90 EUR, four consecutive hours 18.90 EUR. Free with the Magic Pass, including access to the Morond chairlift and bike park. The park opens 1 May 2026 on weekends and public holidays, runs daily from 27 June to 30 August, then returns to weekends in September.

Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 28 September (published 2026 bike-park dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:30
Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.

