Trails
Three mountains, high alpine terrain and a park that leans towards long, sustained descents rather than lap-the-jump-line repetition. Sunburst is the gravity hub; the cross-country network above the village is genuinely worth a day of its own. Quieter and cheaper than Whistler, with the same dry interior dirt as SilverStar two hours away.

Getting up / price
The Sunburst Express chairlift from the village at 1260 m. Adult day ticket 82 CAD at the window, up to 35% less booked online in advance.

