Trails
The biggest gravity operation in eastern Canada after Bromont, and the one with the most vertical: 610 m from the summit to the pedestrian village, on Laurentian granite that stays technical in the wet. The network mixes machine-built flow on the lower mountain with rooty, rocky natural lines up top, and the cross-country trails around Lac Tremblant run for kilometres.

Getting up / price
The Telecabine Express gondola from the village at 260 m. Summer bike ticket prices are sold through the resort and we could not confirm a 2026 adult rate; check tremblant.ca.

