    <desc>Mont Sainte-Cecile 895 m - pedal-access trail centre near Lac-Megantic

Trails
A young purpose-built network on a forested Appalachian mountain, with about 12 km of trails open by 2025 and further expansion underway. Five descents, one climbing trail and two traverses use roughly 285 m of vertical. The lower mountain has easier family and progression terrain plus a pump track; the south summit has intermediate and difficult trails; the north summit descents are very difficult and aimed at expert riders.

Getting up / price
No lift: climb the signed ascent under your own power. Trail access is paid, but a current mountain-bike day price could not be confirmed. Bike and e-bike rental is available. Buy access and check conditions on the official Mont Sainte-Cecile site.

Open season
Open from 16 March; closed from 1 December (published 2026 tourism dates). Weather and mud closures can shorten the riding season.
