Trails
A ski hill that turns over to mountain bikes for the green season, with courses laid out by the professional freerider Daiki Takahashi. The range is unusually wide for a small hill: open piste lines that a first-timer can roll down, through to technical built sections that will hold an expert's attention. Mount Fuji is directly above you, which no other park on this map can offer.

Getting up / price
Chairlifts carry riders and bikes from the base at 1295 m. The resort publishes its green-season lift rates seasonally and we could not confirm a 2026 figure, so check fujiten.net before travelling.

