    <desc>Parque Estatal Monte Alto 2120 m - the main trail area

Trails
Mexico's best-known mountain-bike town, an hour and a half west of Mexico City above a lake. Monte Alto is the marked and maintained core - pine and oak forest, well signed, views down onto the town - and there are seven distinct riding areas around the valley in total, from beginner loops to steep downhill used for national races.

Getting up / price
No lift. Local operators run vans up from the town centre and pick you up at the bottom; you can also pedal, since the climb from the lake is only a few hundred metres. Trail access itself is free.

Open season
Open from 1 November; closed from 1 June (typical window; check the operator and conditions). The summer rains are the off season.

