  <wpt lat="31.206300" lon="-7.861900">
    <name>Oukaimeden High Atlas Enduro (MA) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Oukaimeden plateau, about 2600 m - High Atlas natural enduro

Trails
A high-altitude base for raw, unmarked descents on mule trails, goat paths and old village tracks rather than a maintained bike park. Guided rides link jeep tracks with technical scree traverses, rock, compacted earth, switchbacks and long singletrack descents through Berber villages and pine forest. A documented one-way Oukaimeden to Asni route is about 33 km with roughly 1785 m of descent and 245 m of climbing; the nearby Asni network has about 37 km of mapped trail. Best for experienced, self-sufficient enduro riders.

Getting up / price
No dependable bike lift. Pedal, arrange a vehicle shuttle, or ride with a local guide from Marrakech. The winter ski lifts are not a bike-park uplift. Carry repair supplies, water and offline navigation; trails are unsigned and route conditions can change after storms or road works.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Remote natural mountain terrain with exposure, livestock and pedestrians. Do not ride blindly through villages or cultivated land, and use a local guide for the larger point-to-point descents.
Open season
Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical riding window). Snow can linger at altitude in winter, while midsummer is very hot lower in the valleys; spring and autumn are usually best.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Marrakech | Car / shuttle | ~1h45
Asni | Car / shuttle | ~1h15

Sources: Bike Morocco High Atlas singletrack, Trailforks Asni region and Oukaimeden-Asni route report. Seasonal dates are an average, not an official opening calendar; check weather and local conditions.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.739450" lon="11.957220">
    <name>Kronplatz - Plan de Corones (South Tyrol) [53 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Kronplatz summit 2270 m - top of the Kronplatz 2000 gondola

Trails
The biggest bike park in the Dolomites, on a free-standing dome with lifts up three separate sides. The Herrnsteig is the one people come for: 8 km and 1300 m of descent from the summit to Reischach, South Tyrol's first designated freeride trail back in 2010 and still the yardstick. Around it sit graded flow and jump lines, and the Furcia and San Vigilio sectors on the far flanks. The 360-degree summit view over the Dolomites is not a bad way to start a run.

Getting up / price
Every summer gondola carries bikes: Kronplatz 2000 and Ried from Reischach at 950 m, Olang from the Valdaora side, Piz de Plaies from San Vigilio. Adult bike day pass 53 EUR, season 325 EUR, bike transport included. The Dolomiti Supersummer pass at 67 EUR a day covers this and the neighbouring valleys.

Open season
Open from 16 May; closed from 12 October (published 2026 dates). Sectors open in stages: Reischach from 16 May, San Vigilio from 19 June, Valdaora from 20 June.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

