    <name>Dolomiti Paganella Bike Area (Andalo, TN) [day pass, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Doss Pela 1770 m - top of the Andalo gondola

Trails
One of the two or three best-known bike areas in Italy, spread over three villages on the Brenta side of the valley. Andalo is the flow-trail heart, Molveno looks down onto its lake, and Fai della Paganella holds the harder, rawer lines. Chairlifts continue to Cima Paganella at 2125 m for the long top-to-bottom runs, more than a kilometre of descent to the valley floor.

Getting up / price
The Andalo - Doss Pela gondola from 1030 m is the main bike lift, with the Albi de Mez and Selletta chairlifts above it. Passes are sold per zone or for the whole area, by the day or by four hours. The operator listed 57 EUR for a full-area adult day in 2025 and had not published a 2026 rate when this was compiled, so treat that as a guide and check paganella.net.

Open season
Open from 18 May; closed from 2 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Andalo opens first, the upper chairlifts from late May.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Trento | Car | ~40 min
Verona | Car | ~2h00

Source: Dolomiti Paganella Bike. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
