Five purpose-built forest loops range from the 7 km Greenwood blue route to the 51 km Castlepook red. Expect long forest-road climbs linked by tight singletrack, fast descents and increasingly rocky, technical sections. The network suits beginners on the shortest loop and experienced riders on the full red circuits.

Getting up / price
No lift: every route is a pedal-powered loop. Trail access is free, with cashless parking charged at the trailhead; rental, bike wash and showers are available.

