  <wpt lat="37.208000" lon="-113.202000">
    <name>Virgin Freeride / Red Bull Rampage Zone [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Virgin Freeride / Red Bull Rampage Zone - Virgin, UT

Trails
Flying Monkey is the documented public expert descent from the southern rim of Smith Mesa north of Virgin: 2.53 miles of narrow, steep and loose trail with sharp turns, jumps, unavoidable obstacles, sudden drop-offs and extreme exposure. It runs through the same broader red-desert freeride landscape used by Red Bull Rampage. Historic and current Rampage competition lines are separate, invitation-only event terrain; do not treat them as public trails.

Getting up / price
No lift. Pedal the Mesa Road / Flying Monkey access roads or arrange a vehicle drop where legal; the BLM recommends leaving vehicles before the access road becomes rough.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Flying Monkey is rated extremely difficult by the BLM. It has 20% or steeper grades, crumbling surfaces and places where a mistake could cause serious injury or death. There are no convenient places to stop or turn around.
Open season
Best from mid-September to mid-May. Avoid wet clay, summer heat and active event or land-management closures.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Virgin | Bike / car | ~15 min to Mesa Road

Sources: BLM Flying Monkey trail description, access and safety guidance and Red Bull Rampage event information. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Flying Monkey</name>
    <desc>Mapped 2.3 km central descent of the BLM's 2.53-mile extremely difficult Flying Monkey trail. Narrow, loose and exposed terrain with jumps, unavoidable obstacles, sharp turns and sudden drop-offs. Geometry simplified from OpenStreetMap way 1101932075 (ODbL) - indicative only; use the BLM directions and follow the trail on the ground.</desc>
