  <wpt lat="44.169147" lon="8.343592">
    <name>Finale Outdoor Region (Italy) [commercial shuttle]</name>
    <desc>One of the world's defining enduro destinations

Trails
A vast coastal network linking Finale Ligure, Pietra Ligure and the limestone ridges above the Ligurian Sea. Famous lines such as Rollercoaster, Little Champery and the NATO Base descents combine exposed rock, old military roads, Mediterranean forest and long technical stages. Finale has hosted the Enduro World Series and UCI Enduro World Cup for years and hosts the 2026 UCI Enduro and E-Enduro World Championships.

Getting up / price
No mechanical lift or unified trail ticket. Licensed commercial shuttles and guides serve different zones, while strong riders can climb paved and gravel roads. Book a local operator because trail openings, legal access and sensible combinations change frequently.

Open season
Open from 1 January with no formal seasonal closure.
Daily opening hours: daylight only
Avoid exceptional summer heat, saturated trails, wildfire closures and event-restricted stages. Some trails are maintained through the Finale Outdoor Region system; support the network locally.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Genoa Airport | Car / train | ~1h15
Nice Airport | Car | ~2h

Sources: Finale Outdoor Region services and trail maintenance and the UCI 2026 World Championships announcement. Confirm current trails and shuttle zones with an authorized local operator.</desc>
