    <name>Blue Derby (Tasmania) [no lift, shuttle available]</name>
    <desc>World-premier purpose-built Tasmanian singletrack

Trails
Thirty-five purpose-built trails around the former mining town of Derby plus the Blue Tier wilderness routes. Famous Enduro World Series stages such as Detonate, Trouty, Kumma-Gutza and Shearpin mix enormous granite boulders, dense fern forest, sculpted flow and technical rock. The network spans genuine beginner loops through elite enduro terrain.

Getting up / price
No mechanical lift and the core trails are free to pedal. Multiple private operators sell uplift laps and longer shuttles for Blue Tier and Bay of Fires routes; prices and schedules vary, so reserve directly with an operator.

Open season
Open from 1 January with no regular seasonal closure.
Daily opening hours: daylight only
Rain can improve some granite-based trails but severe weather, maintenance, fire danger and events can close sections. Check the official trail status before riding.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Launceston | Car | ~1h30
Hobart | Car | ~3h15

