    <desc>Kathmandu Valley's established enduro zone

Trails
Natural singletrack drops from the Nagarkot ridge through pine forest, terraces and villages toward the Kathmandu Valley. Guided Himalayan enduro itineraries use the area for repeated technical descents, mixing flow, roots, rock steps and tight local paths. It is a dispersed shared network rather than a signed park.

Getting up / price
No lift. Specialist operators run guided, shuttle-supported days from Kathmandu; self-guided route finding is difficult and can lead onto hiking paths or private land. Confirm the exact descent and vehicle arrangement when booking.

Open season
Open from 1 October; closed from 1 June (conservative dry-season indication).
Daily opening hours: daylight only
Monsoon rain causes mud, erosion and landslide risk. Give way to walkers, villagers and livestock on every shared trail.

