  <wpt lat="28.783810" lon="83.730495">
    <name>Lower Mustang Enduro (Nepal) [expedition, no lift]</name>
    <desc>High-altitude desert singletrack around Jomsom

Trails
Lower Mustang is Nepal's premier big-mountain enduro landscape: fast dry singletrack, loose rock, exposed jeep tracks and technical ancient paths beneath the Annapurna and Dhaulagiri massifs. Signature objectives include Lupra, Ghyaula Pass and long descents around Jomsom and Muktinath; advanced expeditions may continue toward Thorong La at extreme altitude.

Getting up / price
No lift. Access requires pedalling, hike-a-bike and support vehicles where roads permit. Book a specialist expedition covering permits, acclimatization, guiding, lodging and mechanical support; this is not a trail-center day ride.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Altitude, exposure, wind, cold, remote rescue and rapidly changing trail or permit rules are serious hazards. Acclimatize properly and do not attempt high passes unsupported.
Open season
Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (broad expedition window).
Daily opening hours: daylight only
Spring and autumn are preferred. Winter snow and cold close high routes; summer monsoon impacts are lower than elsewhere in Nepal but flights, roads and river crossings remain weather-sensitive.

Access
From | Transport | Duration
Pokhara | Flight / expedition vehicle | ~25 min flight to Jomsom

Sources: Nepal MTB's Mustang enduro guide and guided Himalayan enduro expedition. Verify permits, altitude plan and transport with a licensed operator.</desc>
