Trails
Two dedicated singletrack trails leave the stadium area and total about 4.2 miles, climbing through forest before rolling downhill. The wider recreation area adds scenic multi-use terrain and views toward the Chugach Range. This is a compact pedal-access trail network, not the proposed downhill ski development on the other side of Government Peak.

Getting up / price
No lift or shuttle. Pedal the two-way singletrack from the chalet and yield to uphill riders and pedestrians. Borough parking is 5 USD per day or 40 USD for an annual pass according to the published trail brochure.

Open season
Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (typical dry-trail indication).
