Trails
Kilema is the designated 19 km route for summit-bound mountain-bike expeditions, climbing through forest and moorland toward Horombo before the immense descent. TANAPA also authorizes a non-summit Shira route. This is a multi-day altitude expedition with carrying and hike-a-bike, not a bike park or casual trail ride.

Getting up / price
No lift. A licensed operator, park registration, guide, porters, permits and expedition support are required. Pricing varies widely with group size and summit plan; independent mountain biking is not permitted.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Extreme altitude, cold, exposure and acute mountain sickness can be fatal. Use a licensed specialist, acclimatize properly and follow every TANAPA instruction.
Open season
Open from 1 June; closed from 1 November (preferred drier-season indication).
Daily opening hours: 06:30-18:00
TANAPA's published general cycling window; summit movement has additional timing rules. Rain and snow can affect any departure.

